course: dictionary
lesson: 4222
title: Graffiti: art or vandalism?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Graffiti means words or pictures painted, sprayed or scratched onto walls, trains or other public places, usually without permission. Sometimes it is legal too: large, colourful street art that someone was allowed to paint.
explain: Read the clues around a word. «In graffiti slang, bombing means spraying lots of tags quickly, usually illegally; it has nothing to do with real bombs.» The words "nothing to do with real bombs" tell you that bombing is a special word used by one group of people, and it means something different from the usual meaning.
explain: Graffiti can be right or wrong, depending on where it is and who gave permission. «Some graffiti becomes so loved that towns protect it behind glass, while others think all graffiti should go» shows that people's opinions are split, so you can think about both sides.
fact: Graffiti means words or pictures painted, sprayed or scratched on walls, trains or other public places, usually without permission.
fact: Street art is graffiti that is large and colourful, and it is sometimes made with permission.
fact: Graffiti on other people's property is against the law, and this damage is called vandalism.
fact: «Jean-Michel Basquiat» started as a graffiti writer in New York, became famous young, and died at 27.
fact: Useful phrases: spray graffiti, covered in graffiti, graffiti artist, remove graffiti.
exercise: What does graffiti mean? | *Words or pictures painted or sprayed on public places, usually without permission | A kind of food made with cheese and bread | A sign that tells you the rules of a park | A quiet place to read a book
exercise: «In graffiti slang, bombing means spraying lots of tags quickly.» What does bombing mean here? | Dropping real bombs from the sky | *Spraying lots of tags quickly, usually illegally | Cleaning a wall very fast | Painting one large picture slowly with permission
exercise: «Some graffiti becomes so loved that towns protect it behind glass.» Why would a town protect graffiti? | Because it is against the law and must be hidden | Because it was painted by a train driver | *Because many people love it and see it as art | Because it is a rule that all walls must be grey
test: Graffiti on other people's property is against the law. What is this damage called? | Street art | A graffiti artist's permission | Public art | *Vandalism
test: Which phrase means cleaning graffiti off a wall? | Spray graffiti | Graffiti artist | *Remove graffiti | Covered in graffiti
exam: Which sentence uses graffiti correctly? | The graffiti was a loud bird flying over the hill. | She is a graffiti of the school. | *The old train was covered in graffiti. | Graffiti is a quiet kind of music that people play at home.
